# 02 - Overview + Setup

## Install Terraform

Official HashiCorp installation instructions:

- [Install the Terraform CLI](https://learn.hashicorp.com/tutorials/terraform/install-cli)

## Install Terraform for window 

- [HashiCorp Developer](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/install)

## AWS Account Setup

AWS Terraform provider authentication documentation:

- [AWS Provider Authentication](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/hashicorp/aws/latest/docs#authentication)

Follow these steps:

1. Create a non-root AWS user.
2. Add the necessary IAM permissions, such as `AmazonEC2FullAccess`.
3. Save an access key and secret key, or authenticate using the AWS CLI:

```bash
aws configure
```

For AWS CLI installation instructions, see:

- [Installing or updating to the latest version of the AWS CLI](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/userguide/install-cliv2.html)

## Hello World

The `main.tf` file contains a minimal Terraform configuration that provisions an AWS EC2 instance.

Run the following commands:

```bash
aws configure
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply
```

### Command descriptions

- `aws configure` — Configure AWS credentials and the default region.
- `terraform init` — Initialize the Terraform working directory and download required providers.
- `terraform plan` — Preview the infrastructure changes Terraform will make.
- `terraform apply` — Create or update the infrastructure described by `main.tf`.

## Cleanup

To remove resources created by this example:

```bash
terraform destroy
```
